{
    "background_story": "Perfect was a majestic Andalusian stallion with a coat as white as snow. His owner, a renowned composer, named him after the beautiful musical term 'arietta', meaning a short, expressive melody. Perfect's gaits were as fluid as music, and his spirit as free as a symphony. He was trained in the classical art of dressage, and his performances were always accompanied by the sweet sound of ariettas. As he danced across the arena, his mane flowing like a river of gold, the audience was mesmerized by the harmony of horse and music. Perfect's owner would often say that the stallion's movements were the perfect embodiment of an arietta - a fleeting, yet unforgettable, moment of beauty.",
